a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands the main ideas and specific information of a complex text on both concrete and abstract topics, including technical issues in a specific field of specialization in written texts in social and work contexts."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le06ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to fall short"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to fail to attain a specified amount, level, or degree"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We will fall short of our expectations. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use when talking about teams."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "full potential"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "succeed as well as you possibly can"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Despite having clear roles and responsibilities, a team will fall short of its full potential. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "team role"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the position that someone has in a group of people who have been chosen to work together to do a particular job"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Dr. Belbin has observed people in teams are likely to take on different \"team roles.\""}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "unbalanced"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " not equal because one person has more influence, power etc."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Teams can become unbalanced."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to categorize"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put \u200bpeople or things into \u200bgroups with the same \u200bfeatures"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: He has categorized those roles into three group."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "argumentative"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "someone who often argues with others or enjoys arguing "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They can be argumentative, and may offend others' feelings. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob05aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "inflexible"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "unwilling to make even the slightest change in one's attitudes, plans etc."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: However, they may be inflexible and can be somewhat resistant to change. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob05aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "detail oriented"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "spending a lot of time, effort, or attention to details"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They are detail-oriented and pay close attention to small details. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le06ob05aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Reason Clauses: <span class=\"italic\">Since</span>, <span class=\"italic\">As</span>, <span class=\"italic\">Just in case</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " There are different linking words you can use to introduce reason clauses. Using this type of structure helps to make your writing and speaking sound more professional."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">Since and As </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">since </span>and <span class=\"italic\">as </span>to introduce reasons that the listener or reader already knows."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Since </span>you're new here, I can show you around the office.</span> <br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">As </span>you've already been introduced to everyone, we can begin the meeting.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"underline\">(Just) in case </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">(just) in case </span>to talk about things that may possibly happen."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I'll send you the outline again <span class=\"strong\">just in case</span> you forget it at home.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Since teams can become unbalanced, it is important to have team members with different styles of behavior or team roles. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "As they are concerned with deadlines, they will push the team to make sure things are completed on time. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "They excel at finding the best approaches in case there are any problems."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They'll push everyone to stay on track just in case the team falls behind."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Simple Present, Present Continuous and Present Perfect Tenses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "It is important not to confuse the name of a verb tense with the way you use it to talk about time. <br/>  A present tense does not always refer to present time - it can refer to the future or the past. Let's review and compare the present tenses."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Simple Present</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">need </span>a coffee.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She <span class=\\\"strong\\\">arrives </span>tomorrow.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Present Continuous</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m having </span>lunch with friends right now.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m meeting </span>her tomorrow for coffee.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Present Perfect</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have seen </span>the movie Titanic.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">have completed </span>all my work.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "When a team <span class=\"strong\">is performing </span>at its best, you'll usually find that each team member has a clear role and responsibilities. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " Dr. Belbin <span class=\"strong\">has observed</span> people in teams are likely to take on different \"team roles.\" "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Since teams <span class=\"strong\">can become</span> unbalanced, it is important to have team members with different styles of behavior or team roles. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Belbin <span class=\"strong\">has identified</span> nine team roles."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They <span class=\"strong\">play </span>a factor in team success. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Work in pairs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a Powerpoint or Prezi presentation about action-oriented roles."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make the presentation 2-4 minutes in length."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain each role: shaper, implementer, completer-finisher."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain the personalities of the people in those roles and give some examples."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain the contributions and allowable weaknesses of each role."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I collaborate with a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create a powerpoint presentation that is interesting."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain action-oriented roles clearly and concisely."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain the different types of personalities in the particular roles."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain the contributions and allowable weaknesses of each role."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "type": "WLC", "_data