, "image": "engenn11le06ob05re2img07.jpg"}, {"time": "100", "text": "When a team is performing at its best, you'll usually find that each team member has a clear role and responsibilities. Despite having clear roles and responsibilities, a team will fall short of its full potential. Dr. Belbin has observed people in teams are likely to take on different \"team roles.\" Since teams can become unbalanced, it is important to have team members with different styles of behavior or team roles. Belbin has identified nine team roles that play a factor in team success. He has categorized these roles into three groups: Action Oriented, People Oriented, and Thought Oriented.", "id": 1, "image": "engenn11le06ob05re2img07.jpg"}, {"time": "37700", "text": "Action Oriented Roles<ul><li>Shapers are dynamic and usually extroverted. They enjoy challenging others to improve and excel at finding the best approaches to problems. They ensure that all possibilities are considered. Shapers often see obstacles as exciting challenges but they can be argumentative, and may offend others' feelings.</br><li>Implementers turn the team's ideas and concepts into practical actions and plans. They are typically conservative, efficient and very well-organized. These are the people who you can count on to get the job done. However, they may be inflexible and can be somewhat resistant to change.", "id": 2, "image": "engenn11le06ob05re2img06.jpg"}, {"time": "75500", "text": "<ul><li> Completer-Finishers make sure that things are completed thoroughly. They are detail-oriented and pay close attention to small details. As they are concerned with deadlines, they will push the team to make sure things are completed on time. They may be described as a perfectionist who is conscientious and anxious. They find it hard to delegate.", "id": 3, "image": "engenn11le06ob05re2img05.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn11le06ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le06ob05re2img07.jpg"}}], "id": 1, "template_override": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": []}]}]}